  "question": {
    "text": "A proton is bombarded on a stationary lithium nucleus. As a result of the collision two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></math>-particles are produced. If the direction of motion of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></math>-particles with the initial direction of motion makes an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>, then the kinetic energy of the striking proton is [Given, binding energies per nucleon of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>He</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>MeV</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi>proton</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi>neutron</mi></msub></math>]",
